      "summary": "Cart – Multiple Notification Message Scenarios (Error, Warning & Success Queue Behaviour)",
      "description": "As a Shopper, I want to see only the most relevant notification in my cart at any time, so that I am clearly informed without being overwhelmed by multiple simultaneous messages.\n________\nThis story covers the frontend behaviour of the page-level notification banner (\nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404\n ) when multiple notification conditions are active simultaneously. The rules defined in this story govern how the banner component (SFCC-404) behaves when more than one condition is triggered — including priority order, suppression rules, and success message replacement behaviour.\nThe single-banner approach has been intentionally designed to reduce visual clutter and maintain the premium cart experience. The design rationale is as follows:\nWarnings (e.g. max quantity) are already surfaced at the product line item level (SFCC-795) — elevating them to banner level when an error or success is present adds unnecessary noise\nErrors should always take priority and win over success messages — a customer who needs to fix something before they can proceed must see that clearly\nA customer does not need to see two success messages simultaneously — promo code success is already confirmed in the input field itself and in the order summary line item; move to wishlist success only needs to be seen once for the customer to understand their item has been moved\nMultiple errors are compiled into a single high-level message with a count, encouraging the customer to scroll through their cart and identify what needs resolving\nCopy for the compiled error message is configurable via Contentful UI Copy content model — nothing is hardcoded in the PWA Kit component. Screen reader announcement rules are covered in SFCC-867.\nCross-dep: SFCC-404 (Page-Level Banner — cart message component), SFCC-867 (Screen Reader Announcement Rules), SFCC-795 (Cart Item), SFCC-250 (Max Quantity), SFCC-282 (OOS and Limited Stock), SFCC-796 (Product Unavailable), SFCC-272 (Remove and Wishlist Actions), SFCC-191 (Promotional Code — Promotions epic).",
