      "summary": "Cart – Screen Reader Announcement Rules for Error & Warning Messages",
      "description": "As a Shopper using a screen reader, I want error and warning messages in the cart to be announced in a clear and prioritised order, so that I am informed of the most important issue without being overwhelmed by multiple simultaneous announcements.\nWhen a cart condition exists, up to three messages can display simultaneously across different areas of the cart: the page-level banner (SFCC-404), the inline product-level message on the affected line item (SFCC-795), and the order summary message (SFCC-274). A screen reader will not automatically read all three — the PWA Kit codebase must define explicit rules to determine which message is announced, when, and in what order.\nThis story defines the screen reader announcement rules for all cart notification scenarios. It does not cover the visual display of messages — each component story owns its own visual treatment. Tim Lavelle to confirm implementation approach and ARIA strategy.\nSingle Error\nMultiple Error",
