      "summary": "Cart – Default Shipping Method BM Configuration (Per Storefront)",
      "description": "As a Site Admin, I want the default shipping method configured in SFCC Business Manager per storefront, so that the correct shipping method is displayed in the cart order summary.\nThis is a Business Manager configuration story covering the setup of the default shipping method that drives the shipping line item label in the cart order summary (SFCC-274). At cart stage, the customer has not yet selected a shipping method — that happens at checkout. Express is the default shipping method displayed across all storefronts. \nThe shipping cost displayed alongside the default method is driven by the free shipping threshold configuration — see SFCC - \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-839\n \nNote: this story covers domestic markets only (AU, UK, EU domestic, US domestic). For international markets, shipping is handled by Global-e and no line item is displayed here.\nThis story covers delivery method configuration in SFCC Business Manager only. Carrier assignment, fulfilment, and dispatch are out of scope — these are handled by NewStore OMS via MuleSoft at order placement.\nAU\nDHL Express\nNext Day\nSame Day\nDHL Express International (note: this is the default for AU international but only at checkout)\nUS\nFedEx Ground\nFedEx Express\nFedEx Next Day\nSame Day\nUK\nDHL Express\nDHL Next Day (9am, 12pm)\nSame Day\nEU\nDHL Ground (Economy)\nDHL Express\nDHL Next Day (9am, 12pm)\nSame Day\nFull delivery modes can be found here - \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/469893121/04.10+Delivery+Options\n \nFull delivery logic will be handled in checkout & delivery epic.",
