      "summary": "Lighthouse performance score + bundle hygiene (unused JS, preconnect, source maps)",
      "description": "Context\nSurfaced by the SIT Gate's Lighthouse CI job (\nlighthouserc.js\n, \nlighthouse:recommended\n preset), running for the first time against a real deployed build (SIT bootstrap, 2026-09-01). Full preset kept as-is rather than narrowed, so these stay visible on every release branch's SIT Gate until fixed.\nFailing assertions\ncategories.performance\n — expected >=0.8, found 0.29 / 0.41 / 0.41 across the 3 LHCI runs. Well below target — this project's own AGENTS.md sets an LCP budget of ≤2s at p75 mobile, so this is a real gap against a stated priority, not just a CI number.\nunused-javascript\n — expected <=0 flagged instances, found 2\nuses-rel-preconnect\n — expected <=0, found 1 missing preconnect origin\nvalid-source-maps\n — expected >=0.9, found 0 (missing source maps for large first-party JS — likely a production build config gap, not a code issue)\nScope\nInvestigate the low performance score (likely unoptimized bundle / no code-splitting yet at this stage — see AGENTS.md's \"Code splitting: prefer dynamic import() for heavy components not needed on initial render\")\nReduce unused JavaScript flagged by the audit\nAdd missing \n<link rel=\"preconnect\">\n for the flagged origin\nRestore source map generation/upload for production builds so \nvalid-source-maps\n passes\nOut of scope\n (separate stories)\ncsp-xss\n — see SFCC-856\nPWA installability (\ninstallable-manifest\n, \nservice-worker\n, \nmaskable-icon\n, \nsplash-screen\n) — see SFCC-855\nerrors-in-console\n, \ninspector-issues\n (best-practices category) — see companion story\nStatus:\n logged as a known, accepted SIT Gate failure for now, not fixed same-day.",
