      "summary": "Cart Item Component UI (Part 2) - PWA Kit Component",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper, \nI want\n to see a consistent and complete cart item tile in my bag, \nso that\n I can review my selections before proceeding to checkout.\nThis serves as a Part 2 to \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-270\n and covers the full UI kit of the cart item component, including error states, warning states, promotional states, responsive behaviour, and accessibility. \nThis is a \nPWA Kit component story focused on UI only\n. It covers the build of the Cart Item React component — the individual product tile that renders for each line item in the cart. This story is UI-only. \nThe Cart Item component renders the following elements per line item: product image, product name, price, colour, size, quantity stepper (+ and - controls), Remove link, and Wishlist link. All data is served from SFCC via PWA Kit. Hover/focus/active visual states are defined in the UI kit and are not repeated here.\nNote: error/warning/promotional text can be configurable. This story doesn’t assume final copy. \nDefault\nError\nWarning\nPromotional / Discount",
