    {
      "id": "19166",
      "key": "SFCC-727",
      "summary": "Implement BM config drift detection (Tier A) — diff engine, orchestrator, scheduled workflow",
      "description": "Context\nFollow-up build story for \ndocs/config-drift-detection-plan.md\n (branch \nfeature/sfcc-725-bm-config-drift\n). SFCC-725 (spike, done) confirmed \n@salesforce/b2c-cli\nsolves the WebDAV download blocker and gives export/import parity with \nsfcc-ci\n. This story builds the actual Tier A drift-check tool and wires it into a scheduled workflow, covering \ndata/core\n and \ndata/vendor\n's in-scope fields (schema/attribute extensions, \nservices.xml\n structure, \njobs.xml\n site+step assignment, custom site preferences, payment/shipping method definitions, OCAPI/SCAPI grants) against dev/staging/UAT.\nOut of scope for this story\n (tracked as separate future stories per the plan doc):\nProd config pull (\nworkflow_dispatch\n behind a protected \nproduction\n Environment, draft-PR generation) — bigger, needs its own review given Prod credential handling.\nTier B scope expansion (URL rules/redirects, customer groups, tax class definitions, permission-grant drift).\nExistence-only check mode for the residual BM-owned category.\nMS Teams notification integration (pending confirmation Teams Workflows/Power Automate is available).\nTest Scenarios (manual — run against a real dev sandbox, no Jest coverage for the orchestrator itself since it needs live network/instance access)\n#\nScenario\nSteps\nExpected Result\n1\nIn-sync instance\nRun \nnpm run data:drift-check -- --env=dev\n against a sandbox that matches \ndata/core\n/\ndata/vendor\n exactly\nZero findings reported; exit code 0\n2\nReal drift detected\nManually change one in-scope custom site preference directly in BM (e.g. a Global-e non-secret preference), then run the check\nFinding reported under \nrealDrift\n with the preference ID, old value, and live value; exit code non-zero; a \nconfig-drift\n GitHub issue is opened/updated; step summary shows the finding\n3\nUndocumented live config\nManually add a new non-secret custom preference in BM that has no equivalent in \ndata/vendor\n/\ndata/core\n, then run the check\nFinding reported under \nundocumentedLive\n, not \nrealDrift\n; does not fail the run (soft report)\n4\nKnown secret never flagged\nConfirm a known secret preference (e.g. \ngeSCAPIClientSecret\n) differs or is live-only\nNot reported at all — confirms the exclude-list works\n5\nJob schedule difference ignored\nChange a job's schedule (cron) directly in BM without changing site/step assignment\nNo finding reported — schedules are explicitly out of scope\n6\nArchive cleanup\nAfter a successful run, check the instance's \nimpex/src/instance/\n via BM or \nb2c webdav ls\nThe exported drift-check archive has been deleted — nothing left behind\n7\nAuth failure handling\nRun the check with an invalid/expired OAuth client secret\nScript fails clearly with an auth error, does not silently report \"zero findings\"\n8\nScheduled workflow fires\nAfter merge, wait for (or manually trigger) the nightly dev workflow run\nWorkflow completes, step summary is visible in the Actions run, and a GitHub issue appears only if real drift exists\n9\nStaging/UAT cadence\nManually trigger the workflow against staging and UAT\nSame behavior as dev, confirming the check is environment-parameterized correctly",
