      "summary": "Avalara Integration — Checkout Tax Calculation",
      "description": "As a\n Site Admin,\n\n\nI want\n Avalara integrated with SFCC\n\n\nso that\n the correct tax amount is calculated per product and jurisdiction at checkout across AU and US Domestic storefronts.\nAvalara (AvaTax) must be connected to SFCC via the SFCC Avalara cartridge to calculate GST, and state-level taxes at checkout for AU and US Domestic. At checkout, SFCC sends each line item with its \ntaxClassID\n to Avalara; Avalara returns the correct tax amount per product based on the tax class, the Shopper's shipping address, and the applicable jurisdiction rules.\nNot in scope: \nUK and EU Domestic uses SFCC native tax tables for VAT calculation, not Avalara and is covered in \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-43\n.\nGlobal-e handles its own tax for international markets (US International, EU International, HK, ME). \nFor AU cross-border orders to New Zealand and New Caledonia, Avalara's Landing Cost feature is active to return the duties cost. It returns two tax_types per line item: Output (GST equivalent) and LandedCost (duty). These are the only two AU destinations where Avalara Landing Cost fires, based on the confirmed \nddpCountries\n configuration from the production AU storefront. Avalara uses the HS code and destination country to calculate applicable duties.\n\n\n\n\nHS codes are sourced from AP21 and synced to SFCC product attributes via MuleSoft. ",
