      "key": "SFCC-271",
      "summary": "Cart Item Component - Quantity Stepper (Increment / Decrement Controls)",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper, I want to increase or decrease the quantity of an item directly from my cart, so that I can adjust my order without returning to the product page.\nThis story covers the \nPWA Kit quantity stepper component\n — the – and + controls that render on each cart line item. It covers the core increment and decrement behaviour, the minimum quantity state, and how the cart drawer and order summary update when quantity changes.\nThis story does not cover the enforcement rules that limit or restrict the quantity stepper — these are handled by dedicated stories:\nMaximum SKU quantity enforcement\n (e.g. limit of 3 units per SKU) — see \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-250\n \nOOS and limited stock enforcement\n (e.g. item goes OOS or available inventory drops below cart quantity) — see \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-282\n \nImage for reference (figma leading):",
