      "summary": "Payments – Split Payment: Backend Logic (GiveX + Adyen Combined Transaction)",
      "description": "As a Shopper, I want to combine a gift card or credit note with another payment method at checkout when my balance doesn't cover the full order total, so that I can complete my purchase using multiple payment instruments.\\n\\nThis is the backend integration story for split payment transactions at checkout. It covers the combined GiveX (gift card/credit note) + Adyen (card/PayPal/Apple Pay/Google Pay) transaction at order submission, including: processing a GiveX call and an Adyen call independently within a single checkout (PAY-040); preventing a customer from purchasing a gift card product using a gift card as a payment method (PAY-011a); hiding the gift card/credit note payment option at checkout when a gift card product is present in the customer's cart (PAY-011b). Error states: if either payment instrument fails the transaction must be handled gracefully — the customer must be informed and able to retry without losing order data (PAY-008). Surface: SFCC/PWA Kit backend. Owned by: SFCC/PWA Kit. Depends on PAY-010, PAY-011, PAY-011a, PAY-011b, PAY-040, PAY-008. Cross-epic dependency: SFCC-74 (Adyen Payment Integration), SFCC-78 (GiveX Gift Card Integration), SFCC-17 (Credit Notes & Gift Cards).",
