      "id": "18715",
      "key": "SFCC-381",
      "summary": "Payments – Split Payment: UI Component (Remaining Balance & Secondary Payment Method)",
      "description": "As a Shopper, I want to see my remaining balance after applying a gift card, credit note, or Retail Rewards to my order, and be prompted to select a secondary payment method if needed, so that I can complete my purchase when my applied balance does not cover the full order total.\\n\\nThis component is the frontend UI for split payment scenarios at the checkout payment step. It is displayed when a gift card, credit note, or Retail Rewards balance has been applied but does not cover the full order total (PAY-011, PAY-029). It renders the remaining balance owed and prompts the customer to select a secondary payment method (card, PayPal, Apple Pay, or Google Pay) to cover the difference. The full payment option (where a single method covers the total) is also supported (PAY-010). Error states: this component must handle failure of either payment instrument gracefully (PAY-008). Surface: PWA Kit / SFCC checkout page. Owned by: SFCC/PWA Kit. Depends on PAY-010, PAY-011, PAY-029, PAY-008. Cross-epic dependency: SFCC-17 (Credit Notes & Gift Cards), SFCC-75 (MuleSoft AP21 Retail Rewards), SFCC-78 (GiveX Gift Card Integration).",
