{"result":"{
  "id": "18750",
  "key": "SFCC-404",
  "summary": "Cart Message Component - PWA Kit",
  "description": "**As a** Developer, I want to build the cart page-level notification banner as a reusable PWA Kit component, so that contextual error, warning, and success messages can be displayed consistently at the top of the cart drawer across all cart states.\n\nThis is a **PWA Kit component story** covering the build, variants, accessibility, and responsive behaviour of the page-level notification banner. The banner appears at the top of the cart drawer and is triggered programmatically by cart logic.\n\n**All banner copy is driven by Contentful** — a UI Copy content model in Contentful which has been built to support success states, labels, and error states. Nothing is hardcoded in the PWA Kit component. Copy can be updated by Zimmermann in Contentful without a code deployment. Note: this story does not assume final copy — all content examples referenced in the ACs are indicative only and are configurable.\n\nThe banner has three states:\n\n1. **Error** — red X icon, red text. Triggered by: fully OOS item (SFCC-282), limited stock (SFCC-282), product unavailable (SFCC-796), invalid promo code (SFCC-191). Current content examples: \"AN ITEM IN YOUR BAG IS UNAVAILABLE\", \"AN ITEM IN YOUR BAG HAS LIMITED STOCK\"\n1. **Warning** — grey info icon, grey text. Triggered by: maximum quantity reached (SFCC-250). Current content example: \"AN ITEM IN YOUR BAG HAS REACHED MAXIMUM QUANTITY\"\n1. **Success** — triggered by: item moved to wishlist (SFCC-272), promotion code has been added (SFCC-191). Current content example: \"Product Name has been moved to your wishlist\" “Promotion code added”\n\nEach state shares the same component structure but differs in icon and text colour. The specific copy for each trigger is configurable via the Contentful UI Copy content model.\n\n*Error:*\n\n![\"image-20260908-034903.png\"](image-20260908-034903.png)\n\n\n\n*Warning:*\n\n![\"image-20260908-034921.png\"](image-20260908-034921.png)\n\n*Success:*\n\n![\"image-20260908-034950.png\"](image-20260908-034950.png)",
  "status": {
    "name": "Tech design",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  },
  "issue_type": {
    "name": "Story"
  },
  "priority": {
    "name": "Medium"
  },
  "assignee": {
    "display_name": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
    "name": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
    "email": "marcel.a.n.navarro@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/482e2e100517026f4980d6455214aa11?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMN-6.png"
  },
  "reporter": {
    "display_name": "Isabel Chaloner",
    "name": "Isabel Chaloner",
    "email": "isabel.chaloner@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e5a0df80fa413e572a441e3890e6a12?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FIC-6.png"
  },
  "labels": [
    "CAI-008",
    "CAI-017",
    "CAI-035",
    "CAI-036",
    "Custom",
    "Squad-A"
  ],
  "created": "2026-08-05T11:18:26.517+1000",
  "updated": "2026-09-09T19:52:39.468+1000",
  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "14143",
      "body": "Hi User:600810992b411b0076aaf4cc User:623a4c25562ab90069f7e510 \n\nAs error and warning messages are all caps, should success be the same?\n\nI know this ticket only covers the cart message component but when a there is an error message displayed how will a screen reader behave. Will it read out all error messages on the page (cart message, item message and order summary)?",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Emma Kirwan",
        "name": "Emma Kirwan",
        "email": null,
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/437c30dd63bbb0ec0a2f7c0d8d556d93?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FEK-4.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-31T22:03:30.103+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-31T22:03:30.103+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "14181",
      "body": "Hi User:712020:c99d37b3-9c93-4347-951d-5ffb32ff1341 \n\nAll error and warning messages should be in lower case - designs have been updated.\n\nFor example: [https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026?node-id=40000257-6983&p=f&t=XzHOI7MA1PM9TsUu-0](https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026) \n\n![\"image-20260901-044146.png\"](image-20260901-044146.png)\n\nRe accessibility, the screen reader wouldn’t read out all three. There are some rules that need to be defined in the codebase to give the screenreader appropriate text to read. I’ve created a placeholder story so we can proceed without blocking this one.\n\n[SFCC-867](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-867)",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Isabel Chaloner",
        "name": "Isabel Chaloner",
        "email": "isabel.chaloner@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e5a0df80fa413e572a441e3890e6a12?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FIC-6.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-09-01T14:42:28.278+1000",
      "updated": "2026-09-01T15:14:20.834+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "14192",
      "body": "Hi User:600810992b411b0076aaf4cc \n\nThanks for confirming the lower case text - the images in the ticket show upper case for Error and Warning, hence my confusion but all good.\n\nAlso, good plan creating the other ticket. \n\nHappy to sign this ticket off.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Emma Kirwan",
        "name": "Emma Kirwan",
        "email": null,
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/437c30dd63bbb0ec0a2f7c0d8d556d93?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FEK-4.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-09-01T20:13:34.268+1000",
      "updated": "2026-09-01T20:13:34.268+1000"
    }
  ]
}"}

