    {
      "id": "17837",
      "key": "SFCC-11",
      "summary": "Cart",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Cart\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the build of the cart page and mini-cart in the Zimmermann PWA Kit storefront. It includes line item display, quantity management, inventory visibility, promotion code entry, order summary, and add-to-wishlist actions. It also covers real-time inventory availability at cart level and the buffer stock and reservation logic underpinning bag behaviour.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nThe cart is a critical step in the purchase journey — customers review their selection, apply promotions, and commit to checkout from here. A well-built cart with accurate inventory feedback and clear order summary reduces abandonment and sets up a smooth checkout flow across all 8 storefronts.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nCart page: line item display (image, name, colour, size, price, quantity, item total)\nQuantity increment/decrement controls per line item\nRemove item and move to wishlist actions\nOrder summary (subtotal, shipping, tax, grand total in local currency)\nPromotion code entry field (single code; auto-applied promotions via SFCC promotions engine)\nEmpty cart state\nMini-cart overlay (triggered on add-to-bag and cart icon click)\nMini-cart: product image, name, price, size, quantity, subtotal, View Bag link, Checkout CTA\nMini-cart: Move to Wishlist and Remove actions per line item\nMini-cart: \"Recommended for You\" carousel and \"Shop the Look\" content section\nReal-time inventory visibility at cart and mini-cart level (per variant)\nLow-stock indicator (e.g. \"Only X left\") below configurable threshold\nOOS notification when item becomes unavailable between sessions\nCheckout CTA disabled when cart contains an OOS item\nReturn eligibility messaging on cart and mini-cart for non-returnable items\nSplit-shipment order summary display (if inventory availability surfaced at cart level — to be confirmed)\nOut of Scope:\nInventory list setup and warehouse/boutique routing logic — covered in the integration layer (MuleSoft/NewStore)\nPromotion rules and pricing configuration — covered in SFCC-18 (Pricing)\nCheckout flow — covered in SFCC-12 (Checkout Flow & Delivery)\nWishlist page build — covered in SFCC-8 (Wishlist)\nBuffer stock configuration in BM — covered in SFCC-4 (Product Catalogue)\nDependencies\nMuleSoft/NewStore inventory feed — real-time stock data must be available at cart level\nContentful integration — for \"Shop the Look\" content section in mini-cart\nAssumptions & Constraints\nNewStore OMS is the source of truth for inventory availability; data synced via MuleSoft\nCart and mini-cart behaviour is consistent across all 8 storefronts with currency and tax display localised per market\nPromotion code supports a single code at a time unless otherwise confirmed\nGuest users attempting to move an item to wishlist are directed to the login page\nCheckout CTA is disabled (not auto-removed) when a cart item goes OOS\nStories which are Cart-related but not in scope for this epic:\nGift Card in Cart will be covered in the Gift Card Epic\nNon-Returnable Messaging will be covered in the Returns & Refunds Epic",
